**How to implement.** The host decides captures per object and `measuredElementOf` goes (001 §N '`measuredElementOf` ("the first bound sample") is deleted, and capture branches are decided per object'; 001 §R 'measuredElementOf … replaced by N objects'; the S8.1 brief: 'TableAndElementRotationView.fs measuredElementOf is deleted'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/BeamLayout.fs`: `detectedBranches` takes `objects : Library.ElementId list` in place of `measured` and answers the distinct branches of `detectorCaptures scene detectors varied objects` (step 253), in their order, so one rule decides both; its doc says so in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`. (a) `measuredElementOf` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:measuredElementOf`) is deleted. (b) `member private model.objectIds : Library.ElementId list` answers the elements bound to a library sample, in scene order: the one place the host says what an object is, replacing the 'first bound sample' scans of `measuredElementOf` and `availableCaptures`. (c) `captureDetectors varied` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:captureDetectors`) answers, for each `BeamLayout.detectorCaptures model.sceneLayout detectors varied model.objectIds` entry in its order, its branch and the detector's `SceneElementIndex`, the detectors being the scene's `Detector` elements, so `chartForRun` and `captureLabel` read the per-object capture. (d) `availableCaptures model varied` is `BeamLayout.capturesFor (BeamLayout.detectedBranches model.sceneLayout detectors varied model.objectIds)`; its no-sample transmitted-only filter is deleted, being the rule's (step 253). (e) The docs of `captureDetectors` and `availableCaptures` say: a detector captures the branch by which its light leaves the last object on its path, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1. (3) `AGENTS.md`, the gotcha 'An experiment runs on the light's real path' (step 252): after 'for each captured branch the DETECTOR on it decides the quantity' it adds that a detector captures the branch by which its light leaves the last object on its path. Nothing else changes. After this step `git grep -n -F "measuredElementOf" -- Berreman/` finds nothing (S8.2's invariant). Every existing capture is unchanged: with one bound sample the last object on each path is that sample. Tests. `BeamLayoutTests`: `a detector terminates its beam: nothing behind it is lit, drawn to, or captured` and `the captures follow the detectors: T behind the element, R on its reflected ray, both when both` pass `[ Library.ElementId "s" ]` as the objects, their assertions unchanged. `ElementMenuTests` (UI): `a detector on the second sample's reflected ray offers R, decided by the last object on its path`: the file's `plateScene ()` with the plate's reflected ray switched off (`ToggleElementRay`), a second sample on the main beam between the plate and the seeded detector, bound through the file's `bind` helper to `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` and tilted to R2 = 30° so it opens its own reflected ray, and a detector placed on that ray (`PlaceOnBeam (…, BeamLayout.OnReflectedBeamOf …)`), each by its semantic message: `availableCaptures` for the FIRST plate offers T, R and Both, where the first-bound-sample rule offered T alone; and the experiment varying the first plate's R2 over 0 … 40° in 5 points with capture Both draws `Intensity (T)` and `Intensity (R)`, whose R value at each x is the S₀ of the second plate's reflected `sampleMuellerSpun` at 30° after the first plate's transmitted one at x (spin 0, 600 nm, each resolved through the model's `materials`) applied to `unpolarizedStokes`, within 1e-9.

**Acceptance.** After the host captures per object, `measuredElementOf` MUST be gone, `detectedBranches`, `captureDetectors` and `availableCaptures` MUST decide each detector's capture by the last object on its path, and every single-sample capture MUST be unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a detector on the second sample's reflected ray offers R, decided by the last object on its path`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fourteen s25 invariants MUST pass.
